course: dictionary
lesson: 14899
title: Recreate: make it like before
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To recreate something means to make it again so that it is like it was before. Think of a model of a Roman fort: you use the same plan and the same kind of pieces, so the new one looks like the old one. The word is built from «re» (again) and «create» (make).
explain: You can also recreate a past event, scene or picture by copying it or acting it out. «The class recreated a Viking market in the hall.» Nobody travelled back in time. They acted out what a Viking market might have been like. Ask yourself: is someone making something again, or copying a moment from the past?
explain: Scientists recreate experiments to check their results. «Sam recreated the experiment to see if the plant would grow again.» If the result comes out the same both times, the first result was probably right. Clues like «again» and «like it was before» tell you that recreate is the word to use.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in «make again» or «copy» and read the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Recreate means to make something again so that it is like it was before.
fact: Recreate also means to copy or act out a past event, scene or picture.
fact: «Recreate a scene» means to act out a moment from the past or from a story.
fact: «Recreate from memory» means to make something again using only what you remember.
fact: Re-create, spelt with a hyphen and said REK-ree-ate, is a different and less common meaning: to relax and enjoy yourself.
exercise: «The class will recreate an old Tudor kitchen for their history project.» What does recreate mean here? | To paint it bright blue | To throw it away | *To make it again so it looks like it did long ago | To hide it under a table
exercise: Mia says, «The scientist will recreate the experiment to check the result.» Why would she do this? | To forget the result | To make the experiment longer | *To check that the result was right | To stop the experiment
exercise: «Ben tried to recreate the painting from memory.» Find and copy the one word that means to make something again. | painting | memory | *recreate | Ben
exercise: «The actors recreated the scene from the old film.» What does recreated mean here? | Cancelled | Hid | *Acted out again, the way it happened before | Painted red
test: «Lily wants to recreate her gran's apple pie from memory.» What does this suggest? | She will buy one from a shop | She has never tasted the pie | She will throw the pie away | *She will make the pie again the way she remembers it
test: Which word in the lesson is spelt with a hyphen and means to relax and enjoy yourself? | recreates | recreate | recreating | *re-create
exam: Which sentence uses recreate to mean act out a past event? | «The children ran away from the playground.» | *«The children recreated the Battle of Hastings in the playground.» | «The children ate their lunch in the playground.» | «The children painted the playground green.»
